meta {
  name: 05 - Staff cannot book a resource of another tenant
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bookings
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{staffAToken}}
  x-tenant-id: {{tenantAId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "resourceId": "{{resourceBId}}",
    "startsAt": "2026-08-01T10:00:00.000Z",
    "endsAt": "2026-08-01T11:00:00.000Z"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: gte 400
  res.status: lt 500
}

tests {
  test("rejects a booking on a resource that belongs to another tenant", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.within(400, 499);
  });
}

docs {
  The caller is a valid tenant A member acting as tenant A (so TenantGuard
  and RolesGuard both pass), but resourceId belongs to tenant B. The
  request must be rejected by a database-level barrier, not just by the
  guards. Requires resourceBId: a resource that belongs to tenantBId.
  The exact status code is not pinned; any 4xx satisfies the request.
  The database-level counterpart is
  supabase/tests/database/002-booking-resource-ownership.test.sql.
}
